\DOC DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS

\TYPE {DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS : term list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Deletes from the goal's assumption list every assumption that does not match
any of the supplied term patterns, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {pats : term list} is the list of patterns to keep: an assumption
survives only if it matches one of them, and all others are discarded. The
retained assumptions {A'} form a sublist of {A} in their original order (and
are renumbered accordingly).
{
            A ?- t
     ====================  DISCARD_NONMATCHING_ASSUMPTIONS pats
           A' ?- t
}
\noindent The number of assumptions removed varies from one to several,
depending on how many fail to match.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the filtering is nontrivial, each application removing
at least one assumption and leaving a single goal with an unchanged conclusion;
all inputs are goals with sizeable assumption lists about machine-state reads.

\ENDDOC
